\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Small fine tori}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{On a cycle of length #{N\ge3} with scalar coefficients,
the vertex at #{x} goes to #{2x} and the edge based there
to #{2x+1}. The two constant coarse cochains, one on vertices
and one on edges, give fine fields supported on the even or
odd sites. Both have zero centered difference. By
\ref{fdip-014X} these span the two-dimensional kernel.
On the original cycle the Pauli centered kernel instead has
dimension #{2} for odd #{N} and #{4} for even #{N}
by \ref{fdip-009Q}.}

\p{The kernel comparisons in \ref{fdip-00OO} use different
carriers. On an all-even torus, \ref{fdip-014S} gives
#{2^n} spin copies of one staggered field for the Pauli
module. On the doubled torus \ref{fdip-014X} identifies one
staggered field with all coarse cell degrees. For equal coarse
periods and scalar coefficients this agrees with the harmonic
count in \ref{fdip-0090} and the summed Betti numbers in
\ref{fdip-00OQ}.}
